WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.790
Crypto moves fast.

2
00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.470
Everyone buys at the top.

3
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.510
Everyone panics at the bottom.

4
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.570
After years in crypto we learned the

5
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.190
hard way that holding through a seventy-six

6
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.110
percent drop is not a strategy,

7
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.510
it is a prayer.

8
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.250
And that most losses do not

9
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.110
come from picking the wrong coin.

10
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.790
They come from deciding with your feelings.

11
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.090
This is the long version

12
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.170
of how Strategya fixes that:

13
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.910
where the strategies come from,

14
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.030
what a card is,

15
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.050
how to read the catalog and the summary,

16
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.060
how to choose a plan,

17
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.080
and how to follow a

18
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.430
card by hand or automatically.

19
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.630
Take ten minutes.

20
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.890
After this, the site has no secrets.

21
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.830
Start with the one idea behind everything.

22
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.160
You need a strategy,

23
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.310
a rule, written down before the market moves,

24
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.560
that says when to be in

25
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.870
and when to be out.

26
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.820
Not a feeling, not a tip,

27
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.810
not a chart you stare at all day.

28
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.700
A rule you can test on years of

29
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.590
data and follow without arguing with it.

30
00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.910
Two sentences we use all the time.

31
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.390
We don't predict, we react.

32
00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.430
The rule does not know

33
00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.790
where Bitcoin is going.

34
00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.530
It waits for conditions to

35
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.670
align and then it acts.

36
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.710
And the second one,

37
00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.370
it is not how much you make,

38
00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.590
it is how much you do not lose.

39
00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.430
Capital you keep is capital that keeps compounding.

40
00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.800
Every number on this site

41
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.430
is a simulated backtest.

42
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.710
The rule applied to past prices with commission.

43
00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:25.070
Never real performance, never advice.

44
00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.030
A good rule is not magic.

45
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.310
It is three things working together.

46
00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.540
Trend filters that adapt to how volatile

47
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:32.960
the market is so the rule is

48
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.990
in the market only when the probabilities

49
00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.730
are in its favor and in cash

50
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.250
the rest of the time.

51
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.750
Volume confirmation.

52
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.510
Price going up is not enough.

53
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.690
There has to be real participation behind

54
00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.830
the move or there is no trade.

55
00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.570
And risk management, which is

56
00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:48.930
where most people fail.

57
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.320
A fixed amount of capital,

58
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.630
a stop outside the strategy and

59
00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.810
no arguing with the rule.

60
00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.630
Our rules were tested across complete cycles.

61
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.880
The COVID crash, two halvings,

62
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.590
the arrival of the ETFs,

63
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.830
bull markets and bear markets.

64
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:06.790
They trade little, quality over quantity.

65
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.110
Being out of the market

66
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.870
is a decision too.

67
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.190
Every Strategya rule was born in TradingView.

68
00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.830
This is what it looks like there.

69
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.870
Green when the rule is in the market,

70
00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.220
red when it is out and

71
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.050
the blue line is the money.

72
00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.780
It goes flat when the

73
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.710
rule sits in cash.

74
00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.190
That flat part is not inactivity.

75
00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.770
It is protection.

76
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.030
That is where we started.

77
00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:29.190
And for a while that

78
00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.270
is what we offered.

79
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.550
A TradingView strategy you had to load,

80
00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.750
configure and watch yourself.

81
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.680
Most people never got that far.

82
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.910
TradingView is a professional tool,

83
00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.070
powerful and intimidating.

84
00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.230
So we did the work on our side.

85
00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.080
The same engine now runs every day

86
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.850
after the close on our servers,

87
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.750
checked against TradingView on every run

88
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.940
and it publishes one thing,

89
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.750
a card.

90
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.490
You never open a chart,

91
00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.190
you read the card.

92
00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.280
This is the Bitcoin card today:

93
00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.110
one hundred percent in cash,

94
00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.390
waiting.

95
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.850
Every card opens with today's position.

96
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.690
It tells you whether it changed today,

97
00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.440
the last change with its date,

98
00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.240
the last trade with its result,

99
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.310
and the live price since then.

100
00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.470
One decision a day,

101
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.230
at the close of the candle.

102
00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.320
No charts, no TradingView,

103
00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.010
no trading background.

104
00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.950
This is built for everyone.

105
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.690
Tap price chart: the daily

106
00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.130
closes of the asset,

107
00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.870
orange while the rule held it,

108
00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.670
green while it sat in cash,

109
00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.710
on the window you choose.

110
00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.810
Now tap the plus,

111
00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.790
and the full card opens.

112
00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.030
First, the strategy against simply holding.

113
00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.770
Same one thousand dollars,

114
00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.950
same start date.

115
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.180
Then max drawdown, the worst

116
00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.870
fall along the way.

117
00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.400
On Bitcoin, the rule's is

118
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.230
a fraction of holding's,

119
00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.970
and that number matters as

120
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.110
much as the return.

121
00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:51.690
MAR divides the yearly growth by the drawdown:

122
00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.030
return per unit of pain.

123
00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.910
The card opens on the window since 2023,

124
00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:58.830
and the longer, harder read since

125
00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.830
2018 is always right below it.

126
00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.570
Then the position history,

127
00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.430
a ribbon of every day:

128
00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.310
orange in Bitcoin, green in cash.

129
00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.230
The replay runs the backtest bar by bar.

130
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.970
At twenty times speed the

131
00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.630
whole thing plays in seconds,

132
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.300
and the gap between the two lines is

133
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.710
what the rule made in this simulation.

134
00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:21.670
The trade history: every trade on one line,

135
00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:23.890
with the cash stretches listed too.

136
00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.590
And the statistics, like a strategy tester,

137
00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.330
each number with its own window

138
00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.910
and its own info icon,

139
00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.570
down to every month and every year.

140
00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.310
The guide has a five-minute

141
00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.910
video just on this card.

142
00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.670
The Catalog is one card per strategy,

143
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.610
in three tiers, and each tier

144
00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.430
includes the ones below it.

145
00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.350
Entry is one strategy:

146
00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.740
Bitcoin, one decision a day,

147
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.030
five dollars a month.

148
00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.620
Intermediate adds fourteen strategies,

149
00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.130
twenty-nine dollars a month,

150
00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.190
and all of them are long only:

151
00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.630
they hold an asset or they hold cash.

152
00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.640
No shorts, no perpetuals,

153
00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.830
no leverage.

154
00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.750
Three things appear here for the first time.

155
00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.230
More assets.

156
00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.350
Ethereum, Solana and SUI as

157
00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.270
single-asset cards we call sovereigns.

158
00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.770
Gold, with PAXG.

159
00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.950
And two stocks, MicroStrategy and Tesla,

160
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.550
volatile enough to behave like crypto.

161
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.240
A faster clock: twelve-hour cards decide

162
00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.910
at midnight and at noon UTC.

163
00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.430
We adapted the Bitcoin rule to that clock,

164
00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.170
and on the common window

165
00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:29.410
BTC 12H earns its place:

166
00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.580
about seventy percent a year against

167
00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.410
fifty-four for the daily card,

168
00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.110
with the same drawdown.

169
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.650
A week ago this card was long Bitcoin.

170
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.390
Today it is in cash,

171
00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.190
after exiting at plus twenty-six percent.

172
00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.110
Faster is not free:

173
00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.190
more decisions mean more trades,

174
00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.200
so every twelve-hour card has to earn

175
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.890
its place against its daily sibling.

176
00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.090
And rotations: one rule applied to Bitcoin,

177
00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:57.140
Ethereum, Solana, SUI and gold at once,

178
00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.520
holding the strongest of them,

179
00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.670
or cash.

180
00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.120
Rotation 12H was the best long-only

181
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.530
product of the last twelve months.

182
00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.550
The Proportional one splits the capital by strength:

183
00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.510
on October seventh its card held three assets,

184
00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.590
the next day only SUI,

185
00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.330
and since the eighteenth,

186
00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:15.870
cash.

187
00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.570
A rotation reports cash to cash:

188
00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:19.860
the result of the whole

189
00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.230
stay in the market.

190
00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.670
Expert, fifty-nine dollars a month,

191
00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.060
adds eight long and short strategies.

192
00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.690
A short is a bet on a fall:

193
00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.010
you sell what you do not

194
00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:31.990
own and buy it back lower.

195
00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:32.980
It needs a margin or

196
00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.270
